## 7. Testing and acceptance criteria

Build a test suite around observable behavior, not just whether endpoints return HTTP 200.

### Document ingestion
- Valid PDF, DOCX, TXT, and Markdown files import successfully.
- Unsupported and malformed files produce useful errors.
- PDF citations use correct page references when available.
- Document deletion cleans up associated vectors and metadata.
- Re-importing or re-indexing does not silently create duplicate records.

### RAG and evidence
- Answers cite passages that actually exist.
- Citations open the correct source.
- Questions outside the selected document scope cannot retrieve excluded documents.
- Insufficient evidence produces an explicit limitation.
- Prompt-injection text in a document is treated as untrusted content.
- Comparison results provide evidence from both documents when claiming a difference.
- Contradiction detection distinguishes direct conflict from context differences.

### Privacy Bridge
- Known email and phone patterns are detected by rules.
- Contextual entities can be flagged by local model assistance when configured.
- Users can correct detections before sanitization.
- Repeated confirmed entities receive stable placeholders within a session.
- Separate sessions do not leak mappings into each other.
- Project-level mapping sharing requires explicit activation.
- Unknown and malformed tokens are never guessed during reconstruction.
- Deleted or revoked mappings cannot be used for future reconstruction.
- Residual direct identifiers trigger the configured high-risk behavior.
- Sanitized exports do not leak original values through supported metadata fields.
- The application does not upload content automatically.
- Reconstruction does not change unrelated substrings or repeatedly replace text.

### Reliability and security
- Missing Ollama service produces a clear, recoverable error.
- Failed indexing can be retried.
- API inputs are validated.
- Logs do not contain original sensitive values by default.
- File paths cannot escape the configured storage directory.
- Application startup instructions work in a clean environment.
- Tests and lint checks run through documented commands.

Use synthetic test documents. Never use real confidential files as committed test fixtures.

