## 9. Version 1 scope and deferred work

### Must ship in version 1

- Local document library
- PDF, DOCX, TXT, and Markdown ingestion
- Local RAG chat with verifiable citations
- Quick chats and persistent collections
- Summaries
- Document comparison
- Structured extraction and CSV export
- Contradiction detection
- Markdown reports
- Local Ollama integration
- Hybrid Privacy Bridge detection
- Editable privacy profiles
- Persistent local mappings
- Manual external-AI handoff
- Reviewed reconstruction
- Privacy inspection and deletion controls

### Defer unless the core features are reliable

- Direct external AI APIs
- Automatic cloud fallback
- Team collaboration and cloud synchronization
- Multi-user enterprise administration
- Browser extensions
- Automatic email or cloud-drive ingestion
- Guaranteed anonymity claims
- Advanced autonomous research agents
- Pixel-perfect sanitized PDF reconstruction
- Complex identity resolution across unrelated projects

## 10. Final engineering principle

Prioritize **trustworthy evidence, explicit data boundaries, and predictable privacy behavior** over feature count.

A smaller implementation that correctly grounds answers in documents and handles sensitive information transparently is more valuable than a large interface with unreliable citations or incomplete sanitization.

Start by inspecting the repository, writing the architecture and threat model, and implementing the smallest end-to-end vertical slice: import a local document, ask a question, retrieve relevant passages, display verifiable citations, and confirm that the process works without sending document content to an external service.

Then implement the remaining milestones in order.